#: What a turn looks like on the exact message that asked for it, and the whole of it.
#:
#: **`working` has no mark**, because it has Slack's own agent-session status instead — a mark for it
#: would say a message had been seen twice. **`stopped` and `failed` have none either**, and that is
#: deliberate rather than missing: the answer rundesk delivers for either of them is the news, and a
#: second glyph beside it is this file having an opinion about a turn it did not run. What they do is
#: take the 👀 down, so nothing is left wearing the mark for a turn that ended.
MARKS = {"seen": "eyes", "done": "white_check_mark"}
SEEN = "seen"
WORKING = "working"
ENDED = ("done", "stopped", "failed")

